00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.772
ALEJANDRO: Congratulations!

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:10.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: The Valley of
 the Kings, 3,500 years ago,</i>

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:16.269 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> the Great Pharaohs
 stopped building
 pyramids as their tombs.</i>

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:21.508 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> They chose these
 secluded cliffs to
 become their cemetery.</i>

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:28.648
<i> Today, archaeologists come
 from all over the world to
 unlock the mysteries still</i>

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> hidden in this
 City of the Dead.</i>

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> It's the first
 day in the Valley for
 Cairo born Egyptologist</i>

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:40.226
<i> Aliaa Ismail and her team.</i>

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.263 line:0%
ALIAA: There's a real
buzz in this place.

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:48.368 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
People are coming from
all over the world, coming
to the Valley, it's amazing.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.938 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm so proud to
have such ancestry.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:56.609 align:start size:91% position:9%
It's one of the most
famous necropolises in
the world and I think what

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.379 align:start size:88% position:13%
is special is that
it comes out of nowhere.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.918 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Over
 300 miles south of Cairo,
 in the heart of Egypt,</i>

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> lie the limestone cliffs
 of the Valley of the Kings.</i>

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:15.895
<i> After 200 years of excavation,</i>

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:21.968 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> archaeologists have
 located sixty-five tombs
 hidden among the rocks.</i>

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:26.672 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> But only one has
 ever been found with
 its treasure still inside,</i>

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:29.976 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> it belonged to the
 Pharaoh, Tutankhamun.</i>

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:88% position:13%
ALIAA: This here is
number 62, Tutankhamun.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:39.018
One of those great
finds of the century.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:45.324 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: British
 explorer Howard Carter
 discovered Tutankhamun's</i>

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:48.628
<i> tomb in 1922.</i>

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:52.565 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> One of his teams
 spotted steps leading
 down through the sand.</i>

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:58.438 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> They led to the tomb
 entrance, buried beneath
 feet of rubble and debris.</i>

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:06.279
<i> What Carter found inside
 inspired archaeologists
 for generations to come.</i>

00:04:10.582 --> 00:04:12.585
<i> Deep inside the mountains,</i>

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:19.259
<i> amid a maze of tunnels that
 bore deep through the rock,</i>

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:26.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Carter reached the tomb
 of Tutankhamun hidden right
 in the center of the Valley.</i>

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:33.039 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Inside, he found
 treasures unlike anything
 ever seen before.</i>

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:41.581 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Over 5,000 priceless artifacts
 including golden statues.</i>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> In the burial
 chamber the Pharaoh's mummy,
 wearing a golden death mask,</i>

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:52.825 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> was placed inside
 a coffin made of more than
 200 pounds of solid gold.</i>

00:04:56.395 --> 00:05:01.801
<i> This intact tomb made
 Tutankhamun the most
 famous of the Pharaohs.</i>

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:06.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Now Aliaa is investing
 this golden Pharaoh's life.</i>

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.708
ALIAA: Wow.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.811
<i> NARRATOR: And why his tomb
 remained hidden for so long.</i>

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:18.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Aliaa's team has been
 scanning and documenting the
 tomb for the last ten years,</i>

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> and they've made a
 remarkable discovery.</i>

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.890 align:start size:91% position:9%
ALIAA: The idea here
is to understand what's
going on when you look at

00:05:24.923 --> 00:05:27.360
the data void of color.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:32.965
<i> NARRATOR: The scans strip
 away the paint on the walls
 to reveal unusual markings.</i>

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:37.536 align:start size:88% position:13%
ALIAA: This was the main
scene, and here is the
3D of the North Wall.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:41.607 align:start size:91% position:9%
So, as you can see here,
the silhouette of an
image and this would have

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.876 align:start size:81% position:19%
been done while
they were painting.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:50.082 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: The images
 show the indented outline
 of the face hidden below.</i>

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:53.719 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> It's caused by the
 tip of the paintbrush if
 you start painting when</i>

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:56.055
<i> the plaster is still wet.</i>

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:59.425
ALIAA: This is why the
brushes would have made a
very light impression and

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:02.862 align:start size:91% position:9%
this allows us to
understand it was rushed.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:07.600
<i> NARRATOR: But why would
 the tomb builders rush
 such an important job?</i>

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:12.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The pictures on the wall
 reveal another set of clues.</i>

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:19.111
<i> Despite becoming the
 most famous Pharaoh
 of Ancient Egypt,</i>

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:23.816 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Tutankhamun did
 not have a lengthy reign.</i>

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:27.453 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> He was only
 a nine-year-old boy
 when he became King,</i>

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:33.025 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> and relied on
 trusted advisors to help
 rule his vast empire.</i>

00:06:33.992 --> 00:06:36.162
<i> As Tutankhamun grew older,</i>

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:39.765
<i> he was known to portray
 himself as a warrior king,</i>

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:43.169 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> riding into battle
 on a chariot.</i>

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:48.674 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> But the boy King suffered
 from multiple illnesses,
 including Malaria.</i>

00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:53.746 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> He was only
 nineteen-years-old when
 he unexpectantly died.</i>

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:58.885
(speaking in Arabic).

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:02.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Aliaa thinks
 the marks her scans reveal
 in the plaster are evidence</i>

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:08.627
<i> of a hurried burial due to
 Tutankhamun's sudden death.</i>

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:13.032 align:start size:97% position:3%
ALIAA: The decorated part
of the tomb is very small,
it's only the burial chamber.

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:15.801 align:start size:81% position:19%
The rest of the tomb
is not decorated.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:19.238 align:start size:84% position:16%
If they had more
time, all of this was
going to be decorated.

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:25.144
<i> NARRATOR: While the tomb's
 construction may have been
 rushed, its treasures were</i>

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:30.450 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> everything a Pharaoh
 could desire to take
 him into the afterlife.</i>

00:07:31.316 --> 00:07:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> So why did this tomb lay
 hidden below a layer of rock
 for thousands of years when</i>

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:40.593
<i> all the other tombs in
 the Valley were looted?</i>

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:47.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> To solve this mystery,
 Aliaa will turn to new
 technology as she moves her</i>

00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:50.670
<i> investigation out
 into the Valley.</i>

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:58.978
<i> 300 miles north, in Giza,</i>

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:05.718 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> in the shadow of the
 pyramids, the biggest
 treasure haul in history</i>

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:12.091 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> is getting a new home, a
 one-billion-dollar museum
 and research center.</i>

00:08:12.724 --> 00:08:18.898 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> When completed, the Grand
 Egyptian Museum will reunite
 all of Tutankhamun's treasures</i>

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:23.669
<i> in one place, for the
 first time in 100 years.</i>

00:08:24.202 --> 00:08:27.907 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
TAREK: Having all of
the pieces from the tomb
of Tutankhamun together

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:33.779 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
in one place, this will
be a fantastic chance
to find new facts,

00:08:33.812 --> 00:08:38.184
new hidden things
about Tutankhamun.

00:08:40.185 --> 00:08:43.689 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> NARRATOR: After Carter
 removed the treasures
 from Tut's tomb,</i>

00:08:43.722 --> 00:08:47.326 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> they ended up
 in museums around Egypt.</i>

00:08:47.859 --> 00:08:53.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Now, for the first time,
 scientists and Egyptologists
 will use modern</i>

00:08:53.832 --> 00:08:57.570 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> technology to
 analyze each object.</i>

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:04.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
TAREK: Some details reappear
and give us new information
about these antiquities.

00:09:05.911 --> 00:09:09.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: But some
 of Tut's greatest
 treasures are yet to arrive.</i>

00:09:13.652 --> 00:09:19.992 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> 300 miles south in the
 Luxor Museum, Eissa Zidan
 is preparing 122 of these</i>

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:24.363
<i> priceless artifacts
 for the move to Giza.</i>

00:09:42.314 --> 00:09:46.685 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Eissa's
 packing list includes one
 of Tut's famous chariots,</i>

00:09:46.718 --> 00:09:49.021
<i> intricate model boats and</i>

00:09:49.054 --> 00:09:54.627 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> a unique head
 of the cow Goddess, Hathor,
 elaborately gilded with gold.</i>

00:10:07.472 --> 00:10:09.107
(speaking in Arabic).

00:10:09.141 --> 00:10:13.879 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: After just four
 hours, Eissa's packing
 suddenly comes to a halt.</i>

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:17.282
<i> One of his teams has
 discovered something
 completely unexpected</i>

00:10:17.315 --> 00:10:18.918
<i> in the storeroom.</i>

00:10:20.653 --> 00:10:24.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> It's an antique box that
 Howard Carter used to pack
 and transport Tutankhamun's</i>

00:10:24.322 --> 00:10:25.992 line:0%
<i> treasures out of the tomb.</i>

00:10:32.931 --> 00:10:36.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: The box
 has been missing,
 presumed lost, for decades,</i>

00:10:36.768 --> 00:10:41.207
<i> and no one knows what
 treasures it may hold.</i>

00:10:43.742 --> 00:10:48.047 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> 120 miles south of the Valley
 of the Kings, near Aswan,</i>

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:52.317 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> a Spanish Research
 Team from Jaen University</i>

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:55.888 align:start position:0%
<i> is hoping to follow in
 Carter's footsteps and make new</i>

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:59.158 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> discoveries that
 could rewrite history.</i>

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:00.693
(speaking in Arabic).

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:05.864 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Professor
 Alejandro Jimenez-Serrano
 heads the largest foreign team</i>

00:11:05.897 --> 00:11:07.399
<i> working in Egypt.</i>

00:11:07.432 --> 00:11:10.502 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Today is the first
 day of the dig season.</i>

00:11:10.535 --> 00:11:12.337
ALEJANDRO: Sorry for the mess.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.741 align:start size:97% position:3%
We are sharing the room,
three researchers of the team.

00:11:15.774 --> 00:11:18.110 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
This is my, my bed,
supposedly the best one.

00:11:18.143 --> 00:11:19.311 line:0%
(laughs).

00:11:19.344 --> 00:11:20.779 line:0%
Sorry.

00:11:20.812 --> 00:11:22.414 line:0%
(coughs).

00:11:22.447 --> 00:11:26.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's amazing to get up
and the first thing that you
see apart from the ugly face

00:11:26.785 --> 00:11:30.356
of your roommates is the
Qubbet el-Hawa, the hill.

00:11:33.158 --> 00:11:37.896 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: Qubbet el-Hawa
 is one of the largest ancient
 burial sites in Egypt.</i>

00:11:37.929 --> 00:11:42.134 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> So far, 100 tombs
 have been discovered here.</i>

00:11:42.167 --> 00:11:46.338 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> They belong to the
 nobles who governed Egypt
 hundreds of years before</i>

00:11:46.371 --> 00:11:50.075
<i> the Pharaoh's buried in
 the Valley of the Kings.</i>

00:11:50.108 --> 00:11:52.778
(speaking in Arabic).

00:11:53.411 --> 00:11:58.350 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Alejandro's mission is
 to hunt for more unopened
 tombs and reveal more</i>

00:11:58.383 --> 00:12:00.920
<i> about these early Egyptians.</i>

00:12:01.253 --> 00:12:03.422
ALEJANDRO: It's difficult
to explain how I feel.

00:12:03.455 --> 00:12:08.393
Not only nervous,
it's exciting, it's
a mix of feelings.

00:12:08.426 --> 00:12:10.863
It's an honor to...

00:12:10.896 --> 00:12:13.199
to come every year.

00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:17.302 align:start size:91% position:9%
Now here comes the most
difficult part of the day,

00:12:17.335 --> 00:12:23.008
to climb the hill.

00:12:23.341 --> 00:12:26.311 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: This is the
 team's tenth year digging here.</i>

00:12:26.344 --> 00:12:27.880
WOMAN: It's so nice
to be here again.

00:12:27.913 --> 00:12:29.348
(laughs).

00:12:29.381 --> 00:12:33.085 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> NARRATOR: There's
 a reason why everyone
 is excited to be back.</i>

00:12:33.118 --> 00:12:37.322
<i> Last year, Alejandro
 found the entranced
 to a sealed tomb,</i>

00:12:37.355 --> 00:12:42.361 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> but his permit
 expired before he
 could explore inside.</i>

00:12:42.394 --> 00:12:46.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
ALEJANDRO: Today
is 40 degrees, and
working underneath the sun,

00:12:46.264 --> 00:12:48.768
today's gonna be tough.

00:12:50.235 --> 00:12:53.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: To protect against
 modern day tomb-robbers,</i>

00:12:53.438 --> 00:12:57.276
<i> they put a steel security
 door to block the entrance</i>

00:12:57.309 --> 00:13:02.214 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> of the vertical
 shaft that leads to the
 sealed burial chamber.</i>

00:13:02.247 --> 00:13:06.151
ALEJANDRO: Well it has been
one-year waiting, one-year
imagining the possibilities.

00:13:06.184 --> 00:13:09.421
I'm very excited.

00:13:17.329 --> 00:13:23.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: In Luxor, Eissa's
 team packs Tutankhamun's
 treasures for the move</i>

00:13:23.501 --> 00:13:27.473 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> to the Grand Egyptian
 Museum in Giza.</i>

00:13:29.407 --> 00:13:30.742
<i> But in the storeroom,</i>

00:13:30.775 --> 00:13:34.980 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Eissa is ready to open
 Carter's long-lost
 box to discover</i>

00:13:35.013 --> 00:13:36.515
<i> what's inside.</i>

00:13:43.388 --> 00:13:47.226 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The team gathers
 around to see if the box
 really does contain priceless</i>

00:13:47.259 --> 00:13:50.196 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> treasures from
 Tutankhamun's tomb.</i>

00:13:53.265 --> 00:13:54.533
MOHAMMAD: Ah.

00:13:54.566 --> 00:13:56.501
(laughter)

00:13:56.534 --> 00:13:58.570 align:start size:88% position:13%
MAN: Fantastic.
MOHAMMAD: It's amazing.

00:13:58.603 --> 00:14:02.041 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: These
 delicate wooden pieces
 are ancient boat parts.</i>

00:14:08.513 --> 00:14:12.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Storeroom
 records suggest they could
 be missing from a model boat</i>

00:14:12.417 --> 00:14:15.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Howard Carter
 found in Tutankhamun's tomb.</i>

00:14:27.132 --> 00:14:29.468
<i> NARRATOR: According to
 ancient Egyptian belief,</i>

00:14:29.501 --> 00:14:32.704 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> boats played a
 key role after death.</i>

00:14:32.737 --> 00:14:38.577 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> So, placing model boats
 into tombs was a vital
 part of any burial.</i>

00:14:39.577 --> 00:14:44.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The vessels also came
 complete with crew because
 it was believed the replicas</i>

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:48.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> would come to life
 and help with fishing and
 transport in the underworld.</i>

00:14:51.222 --> 00:14:56.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The Pharaohs used a
 special vessel to sail
 across the sky for eternity.</i>

00:14:57.729 --> 00:15:02.401 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Ordinary people also
 thought they could reach
 the afterlife by boat,</i>

00:15:02.434 --> 00:15:06.272 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> rowing on the Nile
 and into the next world.</i>

00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:12.210
MOHAMMAD: You can see here
the date of the newspaper,

00:15:12.243 --> 00:15:15.047 align:start size:78% position:22%
it's Sunday 5th
of November, 1933.

00:15:22.988 --> 00:15:25.123 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: To discover
 where these pieces came from,</i>

00:15:25.156 --> 00:15:28.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Mohammad inspects
 Carter's original inventory.</i>

00:15:39.771 --> 00:15:44.443 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> NARRATOR: Records
 show that the box was
 sent to Luxor in 1973</i>

00:15:44.776 --> 00:15:47.179
<i> but had gone missing,
 presumed lost or stolen.</i>

00:15:55.487 --> 00:16:01.327 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Eissa thinks
 the rest of the boat is
 safe in the new Cairo lab,</i>

00:16:01.659 --> 00:16:04.330
<i> so they may finally
 be able to reunite it.</i>

00:16:07.132 --> 00:16:09.534 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> To transport
 the treasures to Giza,</i>

00:16:09.567 --> 00:16:14.139 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Eissa's team must
 traverse 400 miles
 of barren desert roads</i>

00:16:14.172 --> 00:16:19.345
<i> and crowded city streets
 before they reach the
 safety of the new museum.</i>

00:16:21.246 --> 00:16:26.485
<i> It will take two trucks
 to transport all 122 of
 the artifacts to Giza.</i>

00:16:27.419 --> 00:16:30.689 align:start size:81% position:19%
EISSA: This a very,
very big moment
for the collection,

00:16:30.722 --> 00:16:32.624 align:start size:81% position:19%
this is the final
trip of Tutankhamun.

00:16:34.359 --> 00:16:37.662
<i> NARRATOR: But with such
 priceless relics on board,</i>

00:16:37.695 --> 00:16:42.634 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> there's concern
 the convoy could be a
 target for a hijacking.</i>

00:16:42.667 --> 00:16:46.238
EISSA: We have a good
police and good army.

00:16:46.271 --> 00:16:51.343 align:start size:88% position:13%
They will follow us
during moving from Luxor
until arrive to Cairo.

00:16:51.376 --> 00:16:55.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: With security
 in place, it's time to roll.</i>

00:16:59.451 --> 00:17:03.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> They now face a
 grueling twelve-hour journey
 through the desert to</i>

00:17:03.421 --> 00:17:06.158
<i> reach Giza before nightfall.</i>

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:14.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Ever since Carter's
 discovery of Tutankhamun's
 priceless golden treasures,</i>

00:17:14.599 --> 00:17:20.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> archaeologists have
 continued to try and figure
 out where and how the</i>

00:17:20.738 --> 00:17:25.811
<i> ancient Egyptians found
 vast quantities of gold.</i>

00:17:29.681 --> 00:17:32.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Fifty-miles south
