waiting for, a traffic signal?

00:17:53.505 --> 00:17:59.211
<i> NARRATOR: The Eastern Desert
 covers 85,000 square-miles
 of remote barren wilderness.</i>

00:17:59.844 --> 00:18:04.249
<i> Some of the rock here
 contains tiny grains
 of gold locked inside.</i>

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:09.454 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Thomas has studied ancient
 gold mining techniques
 for seven years.</i>

00:18:09.487 --> 00:18:12.691
<i> Now he wants to see if he
 can find any evidence of it.</i>

00:18:12.724 --> 00:18:17.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> But this part of the desert
 is a risky place to be.</i>

00:18:18.363 --> 00:18:21.533 align:start position:0%
THOMAS: The thing is we
need to leave before dark
because it's not safe if we are

00:18:21.566 --> 00:18:25.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
staying there because
we can lose our way,
we can have an accident and

00:18:25.537 --> 00:18:29.274 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's also at
the sunset that all the
snakes are going out.

00:18:29.307 --> 00:18:30.775
JOHN: Snakes?

00:18:30.808 --> 00:18:32.210
THOMAS: Yeah, vipers.

00:18:32.243 --> 00:18:33.345
JOHN: No one told me about...

00:18:33.378 --> 00:18:38.584 align:start size:81% position:19%
THOMAS: There are
horrid vipers, yeah.

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:42.621
<i> NARRATOR: The first
 stop, an ancient well.</i>

00:18:42.954 --> 00:18:46.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> It could provide
 clues to the location
 of mining communities during</i>

00:18:46.591 --> 00:18:48.560
<i> the time of Tutankhamun.</i>

00:18:49.727 --> 00:18:51.730
THOMAS: This is the well just
right in front of us here.

00:18:51.763 --> 00:18:54.533
JOHN: It's dry.

00:18:54.566 --> 00:18:56.602
My God, that's
a long way down.

00:18:57.835 --> 00:19:00.705 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: The well
 might be dry today,
 but it was so important to</i>

00:19:00.738 --> 00:19:04.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> the ancient
 Egyptians, they built
 a temple to honor it.</i>

00:19:04.442 --> 00:19:05.944
JOHN: It's beautiful isn't it?

00:19:05.977 --> 00:19:10.282 align:start size:91% position:9%
They actually applied
a plaster gyp ceiling and
then applied the paint.

00:19:10.315 --> 00:19:12.417
Amazing.

00:19:15.553 --> 00:19:18.990 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: The text
 engraved on these walls
 reveals clues about the</i>

00:19:19.023 --> 00:19:21.560 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> gold miners and
 where they were heading.</i>

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:30.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Ancient engineers built
 a network of wells and rest
 stops stretching all the way</i>

00:19:30.368 --> 00:19:34.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> across the desert, each
 a day's walk from the last,</i>

00:19:37.542 --> 00:19:39.644
<i> enabling travelers and miners</i>

00:19:39.677 --> 00:19:43.915 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> to safely cross and
 explore the barren desert.</i>

00:19:43.948 --> 00:19:48.587
<i> The temple carvings
 indicate these wells
 led toward the mines.</i>

00:19:49.721 --> 00:19:52.824 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Thomas hopes he
 will be able to find some
 evidence of the people</i>

00:19:52.857 --> 00:19:56.361
<i> behind Tutankhamun's
 goldmining operations.</i>

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.934
THOMAS: Now it's time
to go deeper East...

00:20:03.434 --> 00:20:06.871 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: Like an
 ancient treasure map,
 they must follow the trail of</i>

00:20:06.904 --> 00:20:09.341
<i> wells further into the desert.</i>

00:20:15.913 --> 00:20:19.251 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> In Aswan, at the ancient
 burial site of Qubbet el-Hawa,</i>

00:20:19.284 --> 00:20:23.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Alejandro is about to
 open a 4,000-year-old tomb.</i>

00:20:24.889 --> 00:20:28.660 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> They're on the hunt
 for whatever burial
 treasure may be inside.</i>

00:20:29.627 --> 00:20:32.698 align:start size:88% position:13%
ALEJANDRO:
I don't know who is more
nervous, me or my team.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:40.472
I want to go now!

00:20:40.505 --> 00:20:41.673
(laughs).

00:20:47.478 --> 00:20:51.549 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: After a year
 of waiting, Alejandro can
 finally enter the tomb.</i>

00:20:51.582 --> 00:20:53.619
ALEJANDRO: It's amazing.

00:20:55.019 --> 00:20:58.590
<i> NARRATOR: It contains a
 4,000-year-old coffin.</i>

00:20:58.623 --> 00:21:03.595 align:start size:91% position:9%
