00:22:48.833 --> 00:22:52.404 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> Sara sprays on a
 liquid adhesive to
 hold them together.</i>

00:22:54.205 --> 00:22:58.510 align:start size:91% position:9%
ALEJANDRO: So, we
will see if they are
capable to make a miracle.

00:23:05.082 --> 00:23:08.219 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: They prepare
 a foam-lined cradle to
 support the boat for the move</i>

00:23:08.252 --> 00:23:14.760 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> to the team's restoration lab,
 but the wooden hull is
 stuck to the tomb floor.</i>

00:23:16.527 --> 00:23:20.432 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> It'll require surgical
 precision using
 scalpels to free it.</i>

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:25.136 align:start size:88% position:13%
ALEJANDRO: From the
tomb to the restoration
lab we are talking

00:23:25.169 --> 00:23:27.505
about perhaps 40-meters.

00:23:27.538 --> 00:23:31.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
But today's very windy which
is very, very aggressive.

00:23:35.847 --> 00:23:38.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: The ancient
 boats are extremely fragile.</i>

00:23:45.156 --> 00:23:47.559
ALEJANDRO: Get ready.

00:23:47.592 --> 00:23:52.030
<i> NARRATOR: With a drop in the
 wind, the team sees the chance
 to remove the first boat.</i>

00:24:05.276 --> 00:24:09.548
♪ ♪

00:24:24.328 --> 00:24:27.499
ALEJANDRO: Perfect.
That was exciting.

00:24:28.633 --> 00:24:32.136 align:start size:84% position:16%
One of the best
moments in my career.

00:24:32.169 --> 00:24:37.976
WOMAN: We have 1, 2, 3,
4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 8 person.

00:24:40.177 --> 00:24:45.183 align:start size:91% position:9%
ALEJANDRO: We take
many weeks to clean it and
fix the pieces that were

00:24:45.216 --> 00:24:49.554
broken some centuries ago.

00:24:53.224 --> 00:24:56.928
<i> NARRATOR: While the team
 gets to work on the boat,</i>

00:24:56.961 --> 00:25:01.099
<i> Alejandro can finally
 open the coffin to see
 who and what is inside.</i>

00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:14.846
<i> In the middle of the desert,</i>

00:25:14.879 --> 00:25:17.215 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> the convoy carrying
 Tutankhamun's priceless</i>

00:25:17.248 --> 00:25:22.721
<i> treasures is two hours
 into its journey when
 Eissa spots a problem.</i>

00:25:28.392 --> 00:25:32.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: A thermal blanket
 protecting Tut's golden
 chariot is coming loose.</i>

00:25:33.397 --> 00:25:37.536
<i> If it flies off, it
 could cause a crash.</i>

00:25:41.739 --> 00:25:44.609 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: The unscheduled
 stop in the desert makes
 this convoy,</i>

00:25:44.642 --> 00:25:49.914 align:start position:0%
<i> carrying the world's
 most priceless treasures, a
 potential target for hijackers.</i>

00:25:49.947 --> 00:25:52.217
(speaking in Arabic).

00:26:01.192 --> 00:26:04.929 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Eissa and his
 team are unable to secure
 the loose thermal covering</i>

00:26:04.962 --> 00:26:06.831
<i> protecting Tut's chariot.</i>

00:26:11.902 --> 00:26:13.237
<i> NARRATOR: Removing the cover,</i>

00:26:13.270 --> 00:26:16.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> they risk the
 scorching desert heat
 potentially damaging</i>

00:26:16.407 --> 00:26:22.080
<i> the priceless treasure.</i>

00:26:22.113 --> 00:26:24.049
EISSA: Everything is okay.

00:26:24.382 --> 00:26:27.252
<i> NARRATOR: Now, Eissa needs
 to get the convoy moving.</i>

00:26:34.091 --> 00:26:37.729 align:start size:88% position:13%
HASSAN: We hope to
arrive to Cairo safely.

00:26:47.838 --> 00:26:52.343 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: In the Valley,
 Egyptologist Aliaa
 Ismail is on a mission to</i>

00:26:52.376 --> 00:26:58.350
<i> discover how Tutankhamun's
 tomb and treasures remained
 hidden for 3,000 years.</i>

00:26:59.450 --> 00:27:04.822 line:0%
ALIAA: A lot of robberies
were going on in ancient
times and modern times.

00:27:04.855 --> 00:27:08.726 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
But it seems that this
particular tomb was not found.

00:27:08.759 --> 00:27:10.695
How was it not found?

00:27:14.131 --> 00:27:18.369 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: The ancient
 engineers of Tutankhamun's
 tomb had a plan.</i>

00:27:18.402 --> 00:27:24.008 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Inside the mountain,
 they went to great lengths
 to conceal the tomb.</i>

00:27:24.041 --> 00:27:28.813 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> The Pharaoh's
 burial chamber is located
 26 feet underground,</i>

00:27:28.846 --> 00:27:32.884 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> and is defended
 from the inside out.</i>

00:27:35.019 --> 00:27:39.490
<i> Engineers constructed
 a wall to block off
 the burial chamber.</i>

00:27:39.523 --> 00:27:43.494 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> They filled the
 corridor leading to the
 King with tons of rubble,</i>

00:27:43.527 --> 00:27:49.434 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> before sealing a
 final doorway and covering
 Tutankhamun's tomb with</i>

00:27:49.467 --> 00:27:55.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> a vast amount of boulders
 under earth standard
 tomb protection of the day.</i>

00:27:58.209 --> 00:28:02.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> But when Carter
 discovered this tomb, it had
 more material on top than</i>

00:28:02.913 --> 00:28:05.350
<i> any other in the Valley.</i>

00:28:06.751 --> 00:28:11.990
<i> This may explain how it
 remained undiscovered
 for over 3,000 years.</i>

00:28:13.157 --> 00:28:16.795 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> But how did this extra
 rock and debris get here?</i>

00:28:18.996 --> 00:28:23.034
<i> Aliaa joins German Geologist
 Martin Ziegler to investigate.</i>

00:28:27.338 --> 00:28:30.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
MARTIN: If you want to
understand the evolution of
the Valley of the Kings, you

00:28:30.341 --> 00:28:32.177 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
need to also understand
the evolution of the rock.

00:28:33.277 --> 00:28:35.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Martin
 thinks there could be clues
 in the rocks at the</i>

00:28:35.479 --> 00:28:37.882
<i> entrance to a nearby tomb.</i>

00:28:38.215 --> 00:28:41.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
MARTIN: Just at the
entrance of it, a slab
is just hanging above,

00:28:41.418 --> 00:28:44.189
a rock basically could
fall out of the cliff.

00:28:45.923 --> 00:28:48.926 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> NARRATOR: Egypt
 is hit with dozens of
 earthquakes each year.</i>

00:28:48.959 --> 00:28:53.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> So, Martin's
 installed a seismometer to
 measure any vibrations that</i>

00:28:53.831 --> 00:28:55.900
<i> could trigger rock falls.</i>

00:28:55.933 --> 00:28:58.503 align:start size:88% position:13%
MARTIN: With this one
we calculate it to be...

00:28:58.536 --> 00:29:02.206 align:start size:84% position:16%
weigh about 600 to 700
kilometers from the
Valley of the Kings.

00:29:02.239 --> 00:29:03.908
ALIAA: What if an
earthquake would...

00:29:03.941 --> 00:29:07.979 align:start size:97% position:3%
were to happen like much
closer to the Valley of the
Kings, how would it affect it?

00:29:08.012 --> 00:29:12.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
MARTIN: A very big
earthquake could destabilize
some rock portions.

00:29:12.049 --> 00:29:13.651
So, when you look in the...

00:29:13.684 --> 00:29:17.455
in the history of recorded
earthquakes, the historic
timescales, let's say the

00:29:17.488 --> 00:29:22.026
thousands of years, we have
some records of earthquakes
of that type of magnitude.

00:29:25.529 --> 00:29:30.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: So, could rock
 falls caused by earthquakes
 3,000 years ago account</i>

00:29:30.234 --> 00:29:35.006 align:start position:0%
<i> for the extra tons of
 rock that covered the
 entrance to Tutankhamun's tomb?</i>

00:29:36.073 --> 00:29:39.277
MARTIN: From the geological
past and the historic point
of view, they could have rock

00:29:39.310 --> 00:29:43.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
falls or rock slides
that are triggered by
earthquakes covering tombs.

00:29:44.548 --> 00:29:49.487
<i> NARRATOR: But there are
 no cliffs directly above
 Tutankhamun's tomb, so it</i>

00:29:49.520 --> 00:29:53.825
<i> wouldn't have been hit
 by a direct rockfall.</i>

00:29:56.160 --> 00:29:59.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> How did so much extra
 material travel down the
 valley and completely cover</i>

00:29:59.663 --> 00:30:02.367
<i> the entrance to the tomb?</i>

00:30:03.234 --> 00:30:07.172 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> To solve this mystery
 Aliaa and Martin
 must take to the air.</i>

00:30:15.980 --> 00:30:19.884
<i> Deep in the Eastern Desert,
 Thomas and John are looking
 for evidence of the miners who</i>

00:30:19.917 --> 00:30:23.888
<i> produced the gold for
 Tutankhamun's treasures.</i>

00:30:23.921 --> 00:30:27.625 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> They're trying to find
 a route of ancient wells
 that the goldminers would</i>

00:30:27.658 --> 00:30:30.261
<i> have followed as they
 travelled to the mines.</i>

00:30:31.495 --> 00:30:33.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
JOHN: It's like looking
for a needle in a haystack.

00:30:33.130 --> 00:30:35.032
But I'm losing a few kidneys.

00:30:35.065 --> 00:30:37.068
(laughs).

00:30:38.903 --> 00:30:41.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Seventy miles
 from the last ancient well,</i>

00:30:41.538 --> 00:30:44.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Thomas and John
 head into the unknown.</i>

00:30:45.242 --> 00:30:49.514 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> With their G-P-S broken
 down, they now risk
 getting completely lost.</i>

00:30:50.314 --> 00:30:52.483 align:start size:84% position:16%
JOHN: This piece of
technology is defunct!

00:30:52.516 --> 00:30:55.386
It is not working.

00:30:57.254 --> 00:31:01.058 align:start size:91% position:9%
Look here, it's literally
on the right side.

00:31:01.091 --> 00:31:03.361
So, we are now
at the back end.

00:31:03.394 --> 00:31:05.897
So, we need to turn around.

00:31:05.930 --> 00:31:10.668 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: But after
 two days of searching,
 John thinks they may have</i>

00:31:10.701 --> 00:31:12.970
<i> finally found something.</i>

00:31:13.003 --> 00:31:14.939
JOHN: What's that over there?

00:31:14.972 --> 00:31:17.341 align:start size:81% position:19%
At the base of that
mountain there?

00:31:17.374 --> 00:31:18.877
So, we found it!

00:31:23.681 --> 00:31:26.951 line:0%
THOMAS: Okay, so it looks
that we've found a very
interesting place here.

00:31:26.984 --> 00:31:28.586 line:0%
It's a settlement.

00:31:30.354 --> 00:31:34.158
<i> NARRATOR: It may look like
 scattered stones and debris,
 but to Thomas' expert eye,</i>

00:31:34.191 --> 00:31:37.195
<i> he can see the outline
 of ancient buildings.</i>

00:31:37.962 --> 00:31:41.299 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
THOMAS: We have the huts
where the people were living
and where they were working.

00:31:41.332 --> 00:31:44.669 align:start size:88% position:13%
Yeah, we definitely have
here the evidence...

00:31:44.702 --> 00:31:46.604 align:start size:78% position:22%
JOHN: Oh Thomas...
THOMAS: Here...

00:31:46.637 --> 00:31:49.340 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean people
have been working
here and we see, yeah,

00:31:49.373 --> 00:31:51.208
there are even more over there.

00:31:51.241 --> 00:31:52.709
<i> NARRATOR: As they get closer,</i>

00:31:52.743 --> 00:31:55.379 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> John spots the tools
 the ancient miners
 would have used to extract</i>

00:31:55.412 --> 00:31:57.181
<i> gold from the rocks.</i>

00:31:57.214 --> 00:31:58.649
JOHN: Oh.

00:31:58.682 --> 00:32:00.584
THOMAS: Yeah, that's
the grinding stone.

00:32:00.617 --> 00:32:03.154
JOHN: That's a pounder.

00:32:03.187 --> 00:32:05.189 align:start size:78% position:22%
THOMAS: Yeah,
that's a pounder.
Yeah, exactly.

00:32:05.222 --> 00:32:06.557
JOHN: That's what
they would break...

00:32:06.590 --> 00:32:08.459 align:start size:91% position:9%
THOMAS: Yeah they would...
JOHN: The quartz with.
THOMAS: Yeah.

00:32:08.492 --> 00:32:12.496 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: It's the remains of
 an ancient goldmining camp.</i>

00:32:12.529 --> 00:32:15.599 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
JOHN: I mean how many people
are we talking, 20, 30?

00:32:15.632 --> 00:32:18.703 line:0%
THOMAS: Yeah maybe there were
like families living here.

00:32:18.736 --> 00:32:24.308
<i> NARRATOR: Thomas has
 studied ancient mining
 techniques for years.</i>

00:32:24.341 --> 00:32:29.447 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> But seeing this evidence
 first-hand brings home the
 hardships the miners endured.</i>

00:32:30.714 --> 00:32:33.384
THOMAS: You start from
a piece of quartz like
this and you want to make

00:32:33.417 --> 00:32:35.019
product out of it.

00:32:35.052 --> 00:32:36.420
So, you need to crush it.

00:32:36.453 --> 00:32:39.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have to imagine
how much pain it takes just

00:32:39.590 --> 00:32:42.593 align:start size:88% position:13%
to break a
single piece of quartz,

00:32:42.626 --> 00:32:47.264 align:start size:91% position:9%
doing that like all
day long, in the sun,
pounding and pounding and

00:32:47.297 --> 00:32:49.634 align:start size:91% position:9%
grinding and grinding
and doing that for years.

00:32:55.205 --> 00:32:58.509
<i> NARRATOR: Evidence here
 paints a picture of the
 life of desert miners.</i>

00:33:00.310 --> 00:33:05.549
<i> They cut shafts stretching
 up to thirty-two feet deep
 into the stone in search of</i>

00:33:05.582 --> 00:33:09.420
<i> precious seams of quartz
 rock that contained gold.</i>

00:33:10.287 --> 00:33:13.291
<i> Crushing the quartz was
 a massive undertaking.</i>

00:33:13.657 --> 00:33:17.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Mining experts have
 calculated that a team
 of twenty people would take</i>

00:33:17.327 --> 00:33:22.467 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> a week to process
 enough stone to make
 just a spoonful of gold.</i>

00:33:24.234 --> 00:33:26.337
THOMAS: That's heavy.

00:33:26.370 --> 00:33:28.172
JOHN: Seriously.

00:33:28.205 --> 00:33:32.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: Sadly, there is
 very little evidence left of
 these ancient mines, but these</i>

00:33:32.476 --> 00:33:37.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> settlements provide new
 insight into the communities
 that lived such hard lives</i>

00:33:37.347 --> 00:33:39.283
<i> processing the gold.</i>

00:33:39.316 --> 00:33:42.386
THOMAS: We have all the
material they were using
for sure, that they were

00:33:42.419 --> 00:33:48.325
working here to extract and
process the gold to send it
to the Valley of the Kings.

00:33:48.358 --> 00:33:51.763
JOHN: We've found it.
THOMAS: We've found it.

00:33:56.200 --> 00:34:00.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: In Aswan,
 Alejandro's team prepares to
 remove the coffin from the</i>

00:34:00.604 --> 00:34:02.540
<i> tomb they've opened.</i>

00:34:02.873 --> 00:34:07.078 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Inscriptions reveal it belongs
 to a man called Shemai.</i>

00:34:07.111 --> 00:34:10.281 line:0%
ALEJANDRO: They have
just struck the lid of
the coffin of Shemai.

00:34:11.849 --> 00:34:18.322
Rebecca, you are the first
person that is looking at
Shemai's face in 4000 years.

00:34:22.826 --> 00:34:24.895
(speaking in Arabic).

00:34:24.928 --> 00:34:26.664
Congratulations!

00:34:26.697 --> 00:34:29.167
(laughs).

00:34:30.234 --> 00:34:34.205
<i> NARRATOR: The inner
 coffin is intact, but
 extremely fragile.</i>

00:34:34.238 --> 00:34:39.276 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Alejandro's team has
 reinforced it to try and
 protect the mummy inside.</i>

00:34:39.309 --> 00:34:41.846 align:start size:91% position:9%
ALEJANDRO: It's
difficult to express the
feelings that I have now.

00:34:42.946 --> 00:34:49.454
It's a special moment because
I'm studying this family, and
it's almost my second family.

00:35:00.898 --> 00:35:03.501 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> NARRATOR: In the
 restoration lab,
 the intricate beauty</i>

00:35:03.534 --> 00:35:06.537 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> of the model boats
 is starting to appear.</i>

00:35:07.671 --> 00:35:12.510 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Termites have
 eaten much of the wood,
 but their excrement</i>

00:35:12.543 --> 00:35:17.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> has actually helped hold
 parts of the boats together
 for thousands of years.</i>

00:35:17.447 --> 00:35:21.552 align:start size:97% position:3%
ALEJANDRO: We have some
parts that are still in a very
good state of conservation.

00:35:21.585 --> 00:35:26.824 align:start size:91% position:9%
This head of the man,
it is covered with
excrement of the termites,

00:35:26.857 --> 00:35:30.328
but the wood is still visible.

00:35:31.862 --> 00:35:36.167
<i> NARRATOR: Alejandro has
 spotted a figure distinct
 from the other carvings.</i>

00:35:36.200 --> 00:35:42.540
ALEJANDRO: We can see in the
middle of the boat a yellow
face which belongs to a mummy,

00:35:42.839 --> 00:35:45.877
which would represent Shemai.

00:35:47.578 --> 00:35:51.382 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: This exceptional
 discovery will help
 archaeologists understand</i>

00:35:51.415 --> 00:35:54.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> the evolution of burial
 practices in ancient Egypt.</i>

00:35:59.923 --> 00:36:03.460 align:start size:97% position:3%
ALEJANDRO: I was
dreaming always to
discover something like this,

00:36:03.493 --> 00:36:06.464
and it's a dream that came true.

00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:14.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Alejandro's
 next task is to bring
 Shemai's mummy above ground</i>

00:36:14.271 --> 00:36:17.875
<i> for the first time
 in 4,000 years.</i>

00:36:32.422 --> 00:36:33.857 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: In the
 Valley of the Kings,</i>

00:36:33.890 --> 00:36:36.660
<i> Aliaa and Martin look
 for clues to explain why</i>

00:36:36.693 --> 00:36:39.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Tutankhamun's tomb
 remained hidden for so long.</i>

00:36:42.866 --> 00:36:46.804 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> They've got special
 permission from the Government
 to use a drone to get a unique</i>

00:36:46.837 --> 00:36:49.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> perspective on the position
 of Tutankhamun's tomb.</i>

00:36:49.906 --> 00:36:51.842
MARTIN: There we go.

00:36:54.578 --> 00:37:00.451 align:start size:97% position:3%
MAN: If we look down we
should be over the Tutankhamun
entrance right now.

00:37:08.792 --> 00:37:12.296 align:start size:97% position:3%
MARTIN: Now we can see the
cliffs in the back, and we can
see the central position of

00:37:12.329 --> 00:37:15.266
the tomb.

00:37:15.299 --> 00:37:18.569
And above we can see debris.

00:37:20.737 --> 00:37:25.409 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: Loose rock and
 debris cover the cliffs
 behind Tut's tomb.</i>

00:37:25.442 --> 00:37:30.781
<i> But the drone also reveals
 these flood channels, carved
 into the rock by heavy rains</i>

00:37:30.814 --> 00:37:36.287 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> over thousands of
 years and they could be
 the vital missing clue.</i>

00:37:37.821 --> 00:37:40.924
MARTIN: We think that if we
have flash flooding, that
material can flow down in

00:37:40.957 --> 00:37:43.594
these kinds of channels.

00:37:47.097 --> 00:37:50.534 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: Throughout
 history the Valley has
 been hit by earthquakes,</i>

00:37:50.567 --> 00:37:53.437
<i> and occasional flash floods.</i>

00:37:54.738 --> 00:37:58.743
<i> The flood waters push rubble
 downhill toward the tombs.</i>

00:38:02.612 --> 00:38:07.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Tutankhamun's tomb
 lies in the spot where the
 channels of water converge,</i>

00:38:10.420 --> 00:38:12.657
<i> and dump tons of rock.</i>

00:38:16.927 --> 00:38:21.899
<i> This, combined with stone
 chippings from a tomb built
 above, buried the entrance</i>

00:38:21.932 --> 00:38:27.672 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> deeper and kept it hidden
 for over 3,000 years.</i>

00:38:30.107 --> 00:38:34.378 line:0%
ALIAA: It's very exciting
for me as an Egyptologist
to see Tutankhamun's tomb

00:38:34.411 --> 00:38:38.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
from up here and see how it
fits within the valley.

00:38:38.982 --> 00:38:42.686 align:start size:88% position:13%
It is the prime
location, it is the one
that was most protected.

00:38:42.719 --> 00:38:45.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
He got the most
sheltered tomb of all.

00:38:47.691 --> 00:38:52.563 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: Tutankhamun was
 a boy King who played a
 minor role in Egypt's history,</i>

00:38:52.596 --> 00:38:57.167 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> but because his
 tomb remained hidden
 for thousands of years,</i>

00:38:57.200 --> 00:39:00.804
<i> his treasure was kept
 safe from robbers and</i>

00:39:00.837 --> 00:39:04.342 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> made him
 the legend we know today.</i>

00:39:13.650 --> 00:39:17.488
<i> In Aswan, the team is
 bringing the mummy of
 ancient Egyptian Shemai</i>

00:39:17.521 --> 00:39:21.692 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> to the surface for the
 first time in 4,000 years.</i>

00:39:30.100 --> 00:39:34.438 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> This is the culmination
 of ten years of field
 work for Alejandro,</i>

00:39:34.471 --> 00:39:38.743 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> and an incredible
 opportunity to
 learn more about Shemai.</i>

00:39:50.520 --> 00:39:55.159
ALEJANDRO: Oh 125,
it's quite short.

00:39:57.961 --> 00:40:01.599 align:start size:84% position:16%
My daughter is more
of less like this and
she's eight years old.

00:40:03.467 --> 00:40:09.807 align:start size:91% position:9%
I expected that at
least he would be around
20-years-old or something.

00:40:11.808 --> 00:40:13.644
It has been a surprise.

00:40:13.677 --> 00:40:18.015
I never expected that
he could be just a boy.

00:40:20.951 --> 00:40:25.689 align:start size:88% position:13%
On his coffin it
was written that he was
the person in charge of

00:40:25.722 --> 00:40:28.559
the administration of the store.

00:40:29.626 --> 00:40:34.231 align:start position:0%
Controlling the store,
you control the people
because you decide who is going

00:40:34.264 --> 00:40:36.667
to receive food or not.

00:40:37.601 --> 00:40:41.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: This new
 evidence reveals Shemai
 held a powerful position in</i>

00:40:41.238 --> 00:40:45.075
<i> Egyptian Society at
 a very young age.</i>

00:40:45.108 --> 00:40:48.879 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> He may not have been
 a Pharaoh, but like
 the boy King Tutankhamun,</i>

00:40:48.912 --> 00:40:55.252
<i> his status afforded him a tomb
 and burial goods to ensure a
 safe passage into the afterlif.</i>

00:41:03.793 --> 00:41:07.764 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> It's taken twelve
 hours, but finally
 Eissa and his convoy of</i>

00:41:07.797 --> 00:41:10.768 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Tutankhamun's treasures
 arrive in the city.</i>

00:41:28.952 --> 00:41:30.554
It's very, very,
very exciting.

00:41:30.587 --> 00:41:32.590
We wait for this moment.

00:41:34.691 --> 00:41:36.727
<i> NARRATOR: Tarek Tawfik
 the Museum Director,</i>

00:41:36.760 --> 00:41:39.563 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> is anxious to get
 everything safely inside.</i>

00:41:45.368 --> 00:41:49.773 line:0%
TAREK: The first cradles
have to be taken out, in
order for the Tutankhamun

00:41:49.806 --> 00:41:51.909 line:0%
pieces to start emerging.

00:41:57.080 --> 00:41:59.249
EISSA: Now I can say
I'm very, very happy.

00:41:59.282 --> 00:42:00.851
Mission is complete, yes.

00:42:01.618 --> 00:42:04.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
TAREK: It will be like
unpacking Christmas presents.

00:42:05.989 --> 00:42:11.762 align:start size:97% position:3%
When we get out these pieces
and find out more details
about how they complement the

00:42:11.795 --> 00:42:14.131
whole story of
King Tutankhamun.

00:42:18.068 --> 00:42:22.339
<i> NARRATOR: Eissa's team
 can finally unpack the
 priceless treasures.</i>

00:42:26.710 --> 00:42:30.080 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Scientists and
 Egyptologists can
 now begin to study and</i>

00:42:30.113 --> 00:42:34.051 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> analyze each item in
 their new high-tech lab.</i>

00:42:35.986 --> 00:42:39.557 align:start size:97% position:3%
Top of the list are the
newly discovered boat pieces.

00:42:42.125 --> 00:42:46.863 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
MOHAMMAD: We'll check
now in our database which
of them maybe related to any

00:42:46.896 --> 00:42:48.699 line:0%
of the boats in the storeroom.

00:42:50.400 --> 00:42:54.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: For almost
 100 years, the boat that was
 buried alongside Tutankhamun</i>

00:42:54.704 --> 00:42:58.943 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> to help him travel
 into the afterlife has
 been missing its mast.</i>

00:43:01.378 --> 00:43:05.315
(speaking in Arabic).

00:43:09.052 --> 00:43:10.654
HASSAN: Exactly!

00:43:24.067 --> 00:43:25.769
MOHAMMAD: It's very beautiful.

00:43:28.038 --> 00:43:34.077 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's amazing that after all
these years, we still have new
discoveries and new secrets

00:43:34.110 --> 00:43:38.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
for this golden King,
Tutankhamun.

00:43:40.250 --> 00:43:42.653 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: 100 years
 after its discovery,</i>

00:43:42.686 --> 00:43:44.988 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
<i> Tutankhamun's stunning
 treasure is still</i>

00:43:45.021 --> 00:43:47.091 line:0%
<i> surprising the world.</i>

00:43:50.093 --> 00:43:51.228 line:0%
<i> And the Valley of the Kings</i>

00:43:51.261 --> 00:43:54.998 line:0%
<i> shows why it remains the
 greatest place on Earth to</i>

00:43:55.031 --> 00:43:58.836 line:0%
<i> hunt for the secrets of
 Egypt's famous Pharaohs.</i>

00:43:59.402 --> 00:44:00.404 line:0%
Captioned by Cotter
Captioning Services.

00:44:01.271 --> 00:44:02.740 line:0%
 

